# DocRack-Web — current local integration configuration
#
# Copy to .env.local only when that file does not already exist.
# Docker Compose instead expects .env.docker.local.
# Preserve existing local configuration. Never commit real credentials.
#
# Pages can render without form credentials. Genuine submissions require
# an intended Google Sheet and working ADC. Use isolated test integrations;
# a local server configured with live credentials still writes to live services.
#
# This template describes implemented variables only. Planned Firestore,
# analytics, and sign-in settings will be added with their implementation.

# Required only for persisting demo/support enquiries.
# Use a dedicated development/staging Sheet, not the production leads Sheet.
GOOGLE_SHEET_ID=

# LOCAL ONLY: path to an intended test service-account key, if required.
# On Cloud Run, leave this unset and use the attached service identity.
GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=./secrets/gcp-sa-key.json

# Optional internal-team email notification. Leave both blank to skip delivery.
# On Cloud Run, keep RESEND_API_KEY in Secret Manager.
RESEND_API_KEY=
NOTIFY_EMAIL=

# Optional verified sender override; enable only after provider/domain verification.
# EMAIL_FROM=DocRack <notifications@docrack.ai>
